WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.621
Idea. Juice bar A has three workers who make one hundred and fifty smoothies a day. Juice bar B has five workers who make two hundred. B makes more in total, but each of its workers makes less.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:27.353
Labour productivity is the output made per worker in a period of time. Divide total output by the number of workers. One hundred and fifty divided by three is fifty. Two hundred divided by five is forty.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:34.307
The answer is in units of output per worker, such as smoothies or cars. It is never in dollars.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:45.825
Method. Step one, take the total output for the period. Step two, divide it by the number of workers. Step three, give the answer in units per worker.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:54.123
Why does it matter? If each worker makes more, the wage cost of each unit falls, so the firm's cost per unit can fall.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:01:11.271
Worked example. Here is a real question from November 2023. A firm employs one hundred and thirty-five workers and makes thirty-three thousand seven hundred and fifty units a month. What is the monthly labour productivity? One mark.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:26.847
Divide output by workers. Thirty-three thousand seven hundred and fifty divided by one hundred and thirty-five is two hundred and fifty. Check: one hundred and thirty-five times two hundred and fifty gives the output back.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:37.748
Now the options. A has the right number but in dollars, so it is wrong. B and D come from multiplying. C, two hundred and fifty units, is correct.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:47.887
The answer is C: two hundred and fifty units per worker each month. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:58.459
Common mistake. A common mistake is dividing the wrong way round. Workers divided by output gives a tiny number that makes no sense.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:04.117
Another is choosing an answer in dollars. Productivity counts units, not money.

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:22.912
Your turn. Now you try. A bakery has twelve workers who make four thousand eight hundred loaves a week. Calculate labour productivity. Next year fifteen workers make five thousand four hundred loaves. Has productivity risen or fallen? Pause here and work it out.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:35.824
Answer. Four thousand eight hundred divided by twelve is four hundred loaves per worker. Next year, five thousand four hundred divided by fifteen is three hundred and sixty.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:46.137
So productivity has fallen, from four hundred to three hundred and sixty, even though total output rose. The number of workers rose faster than output.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:55.220
Remember: take total output, divide by the number of workers, and answer in units per worker. Now try the practice questions.
